Housekeeping, found while implementing karr #105 / ADR 0026 and deliberately
not taken there (the ticket's file boundary allowed a NEW file under t/ only).

t/39-yaml-overflow-literal-becomes-a-string.t, section 2, says:

    # The twelve go-yaml really does resolve to a non-finite float. These must
    # NOT move: they are POK-only here, they are type:float to sops, and the
    # gap between the two is karr #105, which this change deliberately does
    # not touch.

and asserts, per token:

    "[$source] still digested as the token -- karr #105, unchanged"

Every assertion in that subtest still PASSES and still means what it says: its
helper yaml_leaf() parses "v: $source\n", a PLAINTEXT document with no sops
section, and ADR 0026 deliberately does not run its walk there. Nothing is
broken and nothing needs to change for the suite to stay green (973/973).

What is stale is the COMMENT. Since ADR 0026 those twelve tokens DO move for a
document that carries a sops section -- they become a float whose digest input
is +Inf / -Inf / NaN -- and a reader of t/39 would take "karr #105, unchanged"
at face value and conclude the opposite. The new pin for both halves is
t/42-yaml-plain-infinity-is-a-float.t, sections 1 and 7.

Suggested: reword the section-2 comment to say that the disjointness it pins is
the PLAINTEXT parse, and point at ADR 0026 and t/42 for what happens with a
sops section. No assertion needs to change. Test lane.
